    {
      "id": "msg-1784707879423",
      "conversation_id": "conv-1784704638069",
      "role": "user",
      "content": "What are the rules for digital evidence in India?",
      "language": "en",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-22T08:11:19.424Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "msg-1784707879438",
      "conversation_id": "conv-1784704638069",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Reference: Digital Evidence Admissibility (BSA & Indian Evidence Act)\n\nThe Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam (BSA, formerly Indian Evidence Act) defines digital evidence rules:\n- Section 63 (Admissibility of electronic records, replacing IPC Section 65B)\n- Requires a signed digital certificate from the officer in charge to authenticate phone records (CDR), ANPR logs, or server logs in court.",
      "language": "en",
      "cited_record_ids": [
        "case-1784704530759"
      ],
      "confidence_score": 98,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-22T08:11:19.438Z"
    },
